<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_6dcf0fb1-99f6-4a1a-8138-d98a3b3e7e1c"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Cattle-trespass</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_bdb6af69-5dc6-4e42-8d6e-68f7298890c8"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The tort of cattle-trespass is
abolished.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e50119b2-329a-48c2-812a-24a28b4870d9"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subsection (1) does not affect:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_ff7b4964-d723-4519-95aa-ffb2c690e102" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the construction of a reference in any Act to a
trespassing animal,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_f50ae1dd-7932-4ac8-9ccd-6fb5c09f86f2" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the tort of trespass committed by a person by
means of cattle, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_00b2ed16-07fc-4e4f-902c-bfeeafa0c2a3" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the law relating to liability of an occupier of
land for death of or injury to cattle trespassing on the
land.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_881d2b22-b92f-4002-854b-47d6311bd461"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_b67b63db-8701-4e89-895d-c57756b3e618"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Distress damage feasant</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The remedy at common law of distress of an animal
damage feasant is abolished.</txt></block></level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b3b66263-1ad7-44a7-a866-84f0b934de10"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 3</b></no><heading guid="_ca39aa28-1585-4928-b146-703c7bc400fe"
id="pt.3-he"><b>Liability for animals</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_23e71ea4-3fb1-49be-82fc-25ac2208ec49"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_d96bbf22-951a-4f1f-a230-72f460db0b07"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Part:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_80cf81b3-cc7e-45b2-beca-2f2e4e28af43"
id="def.liability"><b><i>liability</i></b></defterm> means liability in
damages for tort.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_090df721-de73-4066-8839-fdf43f46a592"
id="def.occupier"><b><i>occupier</i></b></defterm> means, in relation to any
premises, a person who is an occupier of the premises for the purposes of the
law relating to the liability of occupiers for damage arising from dangers to
persons entering premises, being dangers due to the state of the premises or
due to things done or left undone on the premises.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_df8c1e1a-5438-4c5c-be7d-5a57e4e5a75f"
id="def.premises"><b><i>premises</i></b></defterm> means any land, structure
(fixed or movable), vessel, aircraft or other
vehicle.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_15bf1317-c4f8-4fd9-bdac-f0aef79ff93f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_0cd2de0a-bdf5-4e93-8b10-0982e27d7919"
id="sec.7-he"><b>General liability for damage by an
animal</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0875b10b-9bba-4bf4-9bd1-08b5c970af43"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Liability for damage caused by an animal depends
on so much of the law relating to liability as does not include the common law
abrogated by subsection (2).</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3841f3a8-25a5-453d-84ea-a1387ffecfc2"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Any common law qualification, restriction,
exclusion, extension or imposition of liability that had effect immediately
before the commencement of this Act and related exclusively to liability for
damage caused by an animal is hereby abrogated, whether or not:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_5041dc9d-b8db-4d63-90f7-0153e7ca3940" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">it related to the nature or propensity of an
animal or any class of animal, or knowledge of any such nature or propensity,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_68ea4587-2d8a-4de5-a828-632e95ff9319" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">it applied generally or in the circumstances of
escape on to a highway or in any other particular
circumstances.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_cd405681-2b4d-4989-8747-822d9a25ba85"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_d808f4ab-6f38-4d5d-a653-950d5522d125"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Danger from presence or behaviour of animal on
premises</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Where damage results from a danger to a person
entering premises, being a danger due to the state of the premises or due to
things done or left undone on the premises, the liability (if any) of a person
as an occupier of the premises in respect of the damage depends only on the
law relating to the liability of occupiers, notwithstanding that the danger
is, or is associated with, the presence or behaviour of an animal in or on the
premises.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.9">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e29c5665-304a-419f-a43d-ef721c04a206"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>9</no><heading guid="_3eb8952a-6e3f-4873-924c-10dae5ad1f95"
id="sec.9-he"><b>Restriction of rule in <extref type="case"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Rylands v Fletcher</i></name><citation>(1868) LR 3 HL
330</citation></extref></b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The rule in Rylands and Fletcher does not apply
in relation to damage caused by an animal.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.10">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2794a620-42e1-4946-8d17-9c2f7b2f17a7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>10</no><heading guid="_be2b9479-4b3c-42fb-9f18-fbf212833581"
id="sec.10-he"><b>Evidence of breach of duty in certain
cases</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9532c9ee-5bb2-49e4-bc0c-a35d4c0eeee3"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subject to subsection (2), where:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_9e63c06b-bd45-445e-b61a-e25cd0f02bee" id="sec.10-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">an animal is in or on any premises and the
occupier of the premises:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_08b844a9-ca16-4771-b168-7950809d2086"
id="sec.10-ssec.1-para1.a-para2.i">
<no>(i)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">may not lawfully prevent the animal from being in
or on the premises, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_6e92e4ff-a76d-46dd-b8db-e1b629cc3aa7"
id="sec.10-ssec.1-para1.a-para2.ii">
<no>(ii)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in any other case&#8212;has not consented to the
presence of the animal in or on the premises,</txt></block></li></list>
</block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_2c54a2d6-6ea2-4682-83a7-6829aec9399c" id="sec.10-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a person other than the occupier of the premises
was, at the time the animal was in or on the premises, under a duty to another
person to take reasonable care that the other person would not be subjected to
the danger of the animal causing damage to the other person,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_25116ae5-9021-49ce-8d39-90d42442aafb" id="sec.10-ssec.1-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the animal causes damage to that other person
while it is in or on the premises,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">the fact that the animal was in or on the premises when
the damage was caused is evidence of breach of the duty.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_25c3464a-03d6-49c7-aa96-5199ca2091e2"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subsection (1) does not apply:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_600154be-52ff-4a6c-9578-2da593d452b8" id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">where the premises concerned are a place used by
the public as a road or way, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_6bc07891-b8fc-4682-9ba8-ceb2a86334ba" id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">where the animal concerned is a dog or
cat.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 10:</b> Am 1996 No 121,
Sch 3.4.</txt></content>
</level>
</level>


