<attrib name="id" value="sec.10A"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>10A</no><heading guid="_eca7fc48-bfb5-4133-aa4a-ad53b711e067"
id="sec.10A-he"><b>Ownership of deer and feral goats</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10A-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_99ecb6e2-a7d9-4731-9c93-280d6fba0459"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10A-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A deer or feral goat that is held in captivity
may be bought, sold or otherwise dealt with or disposed
of.</txt></block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10A-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7cee0a03-11de-484b-a367-7b498d38e833"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10A-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If a deer or feral goat ceases to be held in
captivity, all property in the deer or feral goat is immediately
extinguished.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10A-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4352ff37-c4f6-4204-8c84-40e115a3bb3a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10A-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If a person captures a deer or feral goat that is
not held in captivity, the person becomes the owner of the deer or feral
goat.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10A-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a0db1c3d-6853-42f3-9474-f6517d01760d"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10A-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this section:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_2260e67b-261b-47af-9e5a-919d2f465509"
id="sec.10A-def.deer"><b><i>deer</i></b></defterm> means a living animal of
the family cervidae.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_6cd229be-65d8-463f-bcd4-e923b87a5afc"
id="sec.10A-def.feralgoat"><b><i>feral goat</i></b></defterm> means a living
animal of the species <i>Capra aegagrus hircus</i> that has become established
in the wild, has not been born as a result of a managed breeding program and
has not been subject to any animal husbandry procedure or
treatment.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 10A:</b> Ins 2015 No
24, Sch 8.4 [2]. Am 2017 No 62, Sch 1.1 [1] [2].</txt></content>
</level>


